,"forks_count":25807,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":5586,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["elasticsearch","java","search-engine"],"visibility":"public","forks":25807,"open_issues":5586,"watchers":76300,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls/44761","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/44761","diff_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/44761.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/44761.patch","merged_at":"2019-07-26T07:34:37Z"},"body":"This pull request changes the `ForceMergeRequest.validate()` method so that it does not accept the parameters `only_expunge_deletes` and `max_num_segments` to be set at the same time. \r\n\r\nThe motivation is that `InternalEngine.forceMerge()` just ignores the max. number of segments parameter when the only expunge parameter is set to true, leaving the wrong impression to the user that max. number of segments has been applied. This PR also changes `InternalEngine.forceMerge()` so that it now throws an exception when both parameters are set, and modifies tests where needed.\r\n\r\nBecause it changes the behavior of the REST API I marked this as `>breaking`. Once this is merged I'll open a follow up PR to add deprecation logging in 7.x.\r\n\r\nCloses  #43102","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/44761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/44761/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"stat